From: QtScript Qt 6 patch set <qtscript-qt6@local.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:46:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Canonicalize the script library path in
 QScriptEngine::availableExtensions()

On macOS the temporary directory is a symlink: /tmp and /var resolve to
/private/tmp and /private/var. availableExtensions() builds the script
subdirectory from app->libraryPaths() (which may keep the /tmp form) and
then walks it with canonicalFilePath()/canonicalPath() (which return the
/private form), so extension discovery can produce mismatched paths when
a process is launched from /tmp. GitHub runners do not hit this because
their temporary paths live under /Users/runner.

Canonicalize the directory after confirming it exists so the relative
paths computed from it stay consistent.
---
 src/script/api/qscriptengine.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/script/api/qscriptengine.cpp b/src/script/api/qscriptengine.cpp
index bb1ad7a..18f7183 100644
--- a/src/script/api/qscriptengine.cpp
+++ b/src/script/api/qscriptengine.cpp
@@ -3872,6 +3872,7 @@ QStringList QScriptEngine::availableExtensions() const
         QDir dir(libPath);
         if (!dir.exists())
             continue;
+        dir.setPath(dir.canonicalPath());
 
         // look for C++ plugins
         QFileInfoList files = dir.entryInfoList(QDir::Files);
